  <section class="subpage-hero section-shell"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">Legal and privacy</p><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p class="hero-lead">How AICloudStrategist handles website enquiries, fit-review submissions and first-party measurement data.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section-shell section-dark"><article class="shell legal-document">
    <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> 10 November 2026</p>
    <h2>1. Who operates this website</h2>
    <p>This website is operated by <strong>AICLOUDSTRATEGIST PRIVATE LIMITED</strong>, CIN <strong>U62020DC2026PTC470945</strong>, using the public brand AICloudStrategist. Registered company information is available on the <a href="/about/">Company Details</a> page.</p>
    <p>Privacy contact: <a href="mailto:contact@aicloudstrategist.com">contact@aicloudstrategist.com</a>.</p>

    <h2>2. Information collected through the fit review</h2>
    <p>When you request a Cloud &amp; AI Cost Fit Review, the form may collect your name, work email, company, role, company website, selected concern, optional message, privacy consent, landing page, referring path and campaign parameters associated with the submission.</p>
    <p><strong>Do not submit billing exports, invoices, credentials, customer data, architecture files or other confidential information through the public form.</strong> It has no file-upload facility.</p>

    <h2>3. How enquiry information is used</h2>
    <p>Information is used to record and respond to your enquiry, assess whether the Cloud &amp; AI Cost Governance Diagnostic may fit, clarify scope, maintain an operational enquiry record, protect the form from abuse and improve the website conversion journey.</p>
    <p>The fit review is a suitability and scoping conversation. Submitting the form does not create a consulting engagement.</p>

    <h2>4. Form processing and service providers</h2>
    <p>Form submissions are processed through Cloudflare infrastructure and may be stored in a restricted Cloudflare KV namespace. A confirmed submission may trigger a Microsoft 365 notification to the configured company mailbox. These providers may process information in locations outside your country under their applicable service terms and safeguards.</p>

    <h2>5. Website measurement</h2>
    <p>First-party session storage may preserve a random session identifier, first landing path, referring path and campaign parameters. The website may record allowlisted events such as page view, CTA click, form start, validation error and confirmed form success through a first-party Cloudflare collector.</p>
    <p>Analytics events are designed to exclude names, email addresses, telephone numbers, messages and form-field values. Existing event records are configured to expire after up to 400 days.</p>

    <h2>6. Sharing and sale</h2>
    <p>AICS does not sell personal information. Information may be shared with service providers where necessary to operate the website, process and respond to enquiries, protect the service, or comply with lawful requirements.</p>

    <h2>7. Retention</h2>
    <p>Enquiry records are retained only for as long as reasonably required for response, business follow-up, record keeping, security and legal purposes. Retention for any later diagnostic evidence must be agreed separately as part of the engagement boundary.</p>

    <h2>8. Diagnostic evidence is separate</h2>
    <p>Submitting a fit review does not authorize AICS to access cloud accounts, billing exports or production systems. If an engagement proceeds, confidentiality, permitted evidence, access, storage, retention, deletion and responsibility boundaries must be agreed separately.</p>

    <h2>9. Your requests</h2>
    <p>You may request access, correction or deletion of information you submitted, subject to legal, security and operational retention requirements. Send requests to <a href="mailto:contact@aicloudstrategist.com">contact@aicloudstrategist.com</a>.</p>

    <h2>10. Security and limitations</h2>
    <p>Reasonable technical and organizational measures are used for the website and enquiry process, but no internet transmission or storage method can be guaranteed as completely secure. This policy does not claim a security certification or provide legal advice.</p>

    <h2>11. Updates</h2>
    <p>This policy may be updated when the website, service providers or operational practices change. The updated date above identifies the current published version.</p>
